#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "The 9-qubit Shor code"
msgstr "Kode Shor 9-Qubit"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we turn to the 9-qubit Shor code, which is a quantum error correcting "
"code obtained by combining together the two codes considered in the previous"
" section: the 3-bit repetition code for qubits, which allows for the "
"correction of a single bit-flip error, and the modified version of that "
"code, which allows for the correction of a single phase-flip error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita beralih ke kode Shor 9-Qubit, yang merupakan kode koreksi "
"kesalahan kuantum yang diperoleh dengan menggabungkan dua kode yang "
"dipertimbangkan di bagian sebelumnya: kode repetisi 3-bit untuk qubit, yang "
"memungkinkan koreksi satu kesalahan bit-flip, dan versi yang dimodifikasi "
"dari kode tersebut, yang memungkinkan koreksi satu kesalahan phase-flip.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Code description {#code-description}"
msgstr "Deskripsi kode {#code-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 9-qubit Shor code is the code we obtain by *concatenating* the two codes from the previous section.\n"
"This means that we first apply one encoding, which encodes one qubit into three, and then we apply the other encoding to *each* of the three qubits used for the first encoding, resulting in nine qubits in total.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kode Shor 9-Qubit adalah kode yang kita peroleh dengan *menggabungkan* dua kode dari bagian sebelumnya.\n"
"Ini berarti kita pertama menerapkan satu encoding, yang meng-encode satu qubit menjadi tiga, dan kemudian kita menerapkan encoding lainnya ke *masing-masing* dari tiga qubit yang digunakan untuk encoding pertama, menghasilkan sembilan qubit secara total.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be more precise, while we could apply the two codes in either order in this particular case, we'll make the choice to first apply the modified version of the 3-bit repetition code (which detects phase-flip errors), and then we'll encode *each* of the resulting three qubits independently using the original 3-bit repetition code (which detects bit-flip errors).\n"
"Here is a circuit diagram representation of this encoding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lebih tepatnya, meskipun kita bisa menerapkan dua kode dalam urutan mana pun dalam kasus khusus ini, kita akan memilih untuk pertama menerapkan versi yang dimodifikasi dari kode repetisi 3-bit (yang mendeteksi kesalahan phase-flip), dan kemudian kita meng-encode *masing-masing* dari tiga qubit yang dihasilkan secara independen menggunakan kode repetisi 3-bit asli (yang mendeteksi kesalahan bit-flip).\n"
"Berikut adalah representasi diagram Circuit dari encoding ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Encoding circuit for the 9-qubit Shor code showing three "
"blocks](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-encoder.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Encoding circuit for the 9-qubit Shor code showing three "
"blocks](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-encoder.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the figure suggests, we'll think about the nine qubits of the Shor code as being grouped into three blocks of three qubits, where each block is obtained from the *second* encoding step (which is the ordinary 3-bit repetition code).\n"
"The ordinary 3-bit repetition code, which here is applied three times independently, is called the *inner code* in this context, whereas the *outer code* is the code used for the first encoding step, which is the modified version of the 3-bit repetition code that detects phase-flip errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang disarankan oleh gambar, kita akan memikirkan sembilan qubit dari kode Shor sebagai dikelompokkan menjadi tiga blok tiga qubit, di mana setiap blok diperoleh dari langkah encoding *kedua* (yang merupakan kode repetisi 3-bit biasa).\n"
"Kode repetisi 3-bit biasa, yang di sini diterapkan tiga kali secara independen, disebut *kode dalam* dalam konteks ini, sedangkan *kode luar* adalah kode yang digunakan untuk langkah encoding pertama, yaitu versi yang dimodifikasi dari kode repetisi 3-bit yang mendeteksi kesalahan phase-flip.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can alternatively specify the code by describing how the two standard "
"basis states for our original qubit get encoded.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita bisa secara alternatif menentukan kode dengan mendeskripsikan bagaimana"
" dua keadaan basis standar untuk qubit asli kita di-encode.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle &\n"
"\\:\\mapsto\\:\n"
"\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\vert 1\\rangle &\n"
"\\:\\mapsto\\:\n"
"\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle &\n"
"\\:\\mapsto\\:\n"
"\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle) \\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\vert 1\\rangle &\n"
"\\:\\mapsto\\:\n"
"\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle) \\otimes\n"
"(\\vert 000\\rangle - \\vert 111\\rangle)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once we know this, we can determine by linearity how an arbitrary qubit "
"state vector is encoded.\n"
msgstr ""
"Begitu kita mengetahui ini, kita bisa menentukan dengan linieritas bagaimana"
" vektor keadaan qubit sembarangan di-encode.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Correcting bit-flip and phase-flip errors {#correcting-bit-flip-and-phase-"
"flip-errors}"
msgstr ""
"Mengoreksi kesalahan bit-flip dan phase-flip {#correcting-bit-flip-and-"
"phase-flip-errors}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Errors and CNOT gates {#errors-and-cnot-gates}"
msgstr "Kesalahan dan gate CNOT {#errors-and-cnot-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze how $X$ and $Z$ errors affect encodings of qubits, both for the 9-qubit Shor code as well as other codes, it will be helpful to observe a few simple relationships between these errors and CNOT gates.\n"
"As we begin to analyze the 9-qubit Shor code, this is a reasonable moment to pause to do this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menganalisis bagaimana kesalahan $X$ dan $Z$ mempengaruhi encoding qubit, baik untuk kode Shor 9-Qubit maupun kode lainnya, akan berguna untuk mengamati beberapa hubungan sederhana antara kesalahan-kesalahan ini dan gate CNOT.\n"
"Saat kita mulai menganalisis kode Shor 9-Qubit, ini adalah momen yang tepat untuk berhenti sejenak dan melakukan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following circuit diagrams illustrate three basic relationships among $X$ gates and CNOT gates.\n"
"Specifically, applying an $X$ gate to the *target* qubit prior to a CNOT is equivalent to swapping the order and performing the CNOT first, but applying an $X$ gate to the *control* qubit prior to a CNOT is equivalent to applying $X$ gates to both qubits after the CNOT.\n"
"Finally, applying $X$ gates to both qubits prior to a CNOT is equivalent to applying the CNOT first and then applying an $X$ gate to the control qubit.\n"
"These relationships can be verified by performing the required matrix multiplications or computing the effect of the circuits on standard basis states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diagram Circuit berikut mengilustrasikan tiga hubungan dasar antara gate $X$ dan gate CNOT.\n"
"Khususnya, menerapkan gate $X$ ke qubit *target* sebelum CNOT setara dengan menukar urutan dan melakukan CNOT terlebih dahulu, tetapi menerapkan gate $X$ ke qubit *kontrol* sebelum CNOT setara dengan menerapkan gate $X$ ke kedua qubit setelah CNOT.\n"
"Akhirnya, menerapkan gate $X$ ke kedua qubit sebelum CNOT setara dengan melakukan CNOT terlebih dahulu dan kemudian menerapkan gate $X$ ke qubit kontrol.\n"
"Hubungan-hubungan ini bisa diverifikasi dengan melakukan perkalian matriks yang diperlukan atau menghitung efek Circuit pada keadaan basis standar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![X errors before and after CNOT "
"gates](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/X-and-CNOT.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![X errors before and after CNOT "
"gates](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/X-and-CNOT.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The situation is similar for $Z$ gates, except that the roles of the control and target qubits switch.\n"
"In particular, we have the three relationships depicted by the following quantum circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Situasinya serupa untuk gate $Z$, kecuali bahwa peran qubit kontrol dan target bertukar.\n"
"Khususnya, kita memiliki tiga hubungan yang digambarkan oleh Circuit kuantum berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Z errors before and after CNOT "
"gates](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Z-and-CNOT.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Z errors before and after CNOT "
"gates](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Z-and-CNOT.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Correcting bit-flip errors {#correcting-bit-flip-errors}"
msgstr "Mengoreksi kesalahan bit-flip {#correcting-bit-flip-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll consider how errors can be detected and corrected using the "
"9-qubit Shor code, starting with bit-flip errors — which we'll generally "
"refer to as $X$ errors hereafter for the sake of brevity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita akan mempertimbangkan bagaimana kesalahan bisa dideteksi dan "
"dikoreksi menggunakan kode Shor 9-Qubit, dimulai dengan kesalahan bit-flip —"
" yang umumnya akan kita sebut kesalahan $X$ mulai sekarang demi "
"keringkasan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To detect and correct $X$ errors, we can simply treat each of the three blocks in the encoding separately.\n"
"Each block is an encoding of a qubit using the 3-bit repetition code, which protects against $X$ errors — so by performing the syndrome measurements and $X$ error corrections described previously to each block, we can detect and correct up to one $X$ error per block.\n"
"In particular, if there is at most one $X$ error on the nine qubits of the encoding, this error will be detected and corrected by this procedure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mendeteksi dan mengoreksi kesalahan $X$, kita cukup memperlakukan masing-masing dari tiga blok dalam encoding secara terpisah.\n"
"Setiap blok adalah encoding qubit menggunakan kode repetisi 3-bit, yang melindungi terhadap kesalahan $X$ — sehingga dengan melakukan pengukuran sindrom dan koreksi kesalahan $X$ yang sudah dijelaskan sebelumnya ke setiap blok, kita bisa mendeteksi dan mengoreksi hingga satu kesalahan $X$ per blok.\n"
"Khususnya, jika ada paling banyak satu kesalahan $X$ pada sembilan qubit encoding, kesalahan ini akan dideteksi dan dikoreksi oleh prosedur ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In short, correcting bit-flip errors is a simple matter for this code, due "
"to the fact that the inner code corrects bit-flip errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Singkatnya, mengoreksi kesalahan bit-flip adalah hal yang sederhana untuk "
"kode ini, karena kode dalam mengoreksi kesalahan bit-flip.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Correcting phase-flip errors {#correcting-phase-flip-errors}"
msgstr "Mengoreksi kesalahan phase-flip {#correcting-phase-flip-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we'll consider phase-flip errors, or $Z$ errors for brevity.\n"
"This time it's not quite as clear what we should do because the outer code is the one that detects $Z$ errors, but the inner code seems to be somehow \"in the way,\" making the detection and correction of these errors slightly more difficult.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya kita akan mempertimbangkan kesalahan phase-flip, atau kesalahan $Z$ untuk keringkasan.\n"
"Kali ini tidak begitu jelas apa yang harus kita lakukan karena kode luar adalah yang mendeteksi kesalahan $Z$, tetapi kode dalam tampaknya entah bagaimana \"menghalangi\", membuat deteksi dan koreksi kesalahan ini sedikit lebih sulit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that a $Z$ error occurs on one of the 9 qubits of the Shor code, "
"such as the one indicated in this diagram.\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan kesalahan $Z$ terjadi pada salah satu dari 9 qubit kode Shor, "
"seperti yang ditunjukkan dalam diagram ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Z error on a qubit for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-phase-error-1.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Z error on a qubit for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-phase-error-1.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've already observed what happens when a $Z$ error occurs when we're using the 3-bit repetition code —\n"
"it's equivalent to a $Z$ error occurring prior to encoding.\n"
"In the context of the 9-qubit Shor code, this means that a $Z$ error on any one of the three qubits within a block always has the same effect, which is equivalent to a $Z$ error occurring on the corresponding qubit prior to the inner code being applied.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sudah mengamati apa yang terjadi ketika kesalahan $Z$ terjadi saat kita menggunakan kode repetisi 3-bit —\n"
"ini setara dengan kesalahan $Z$ yang terjadi sebelum encoding.\n"
"Dalam konteks kode Shor 9-Qubit, ini berarti bahwa kesalahan $Z$ pada salah satu dari tiga qubit dalam satu blok selalu memiliki efek yang sama, yang setara dengan kesalahan $Z$ yang terjadi pada qubit yang bersesuaian sebelum kode dalam diterapkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, the circuit diagram above is equivalent to the following diagram.\n"
"This can be reasoned using the relationships between $Z$ and CNOT gates described above, or by simply evaluating the circuits on an arbitrary qubit state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, diagram Circuit di atas setara dengan diagram berikut.\n"
"Ini bisa dibuktikan menggunakan hubungan antara gate $Z$ dan CNOT yang dijelaskan di atas, atau cukup dengan mengevaluasi Circuit pada keadaan qubit sembarangan $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Z error prior to the inner code for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-phase-error-2.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Z error prior to the inner code for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-phase-error-2.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This suggests one option for detecting and correcting $Z$ errors, which is to *decode* the inner code, leaving us with the three qubits used for the outer encoding along with six initialized workspace qubits.\n"
"We can then check these three qubits of the outer code for $Z$ errors, and then finally we can re-encode using the inner code, to bring us back to the 9-qubit encoding we get from the Shor code.\n"
"If we do detect a $Z$ error, we can either correct it prior to re-encoding with the inner code, or we can correct it after re-encoding, by applying a $Z$ gate to any of the qubits in that block.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini menyarankan satu pilihan untuk mendeteksi dan mengoreksi kesalahan $Z$, yaitu men-*decode* kode dalam, meninggalkan kita dengan tiga qubit yang digunakan untuk encoding luar beserta enam qubit workspace yang sudah diinisialisasi.\n"
"Kita kemudian bisa memeriksa tiga qubit kode luar ini untuk kesalahan $Z$, dan akhirnya kita bisa meng-encode ulang menggunakan kode dalam, untuk membawa kita kembali ke encoding 9-Qubit yang kita dapatkan dari kode Shor.\n"
"Jika kita mendeteksi kesalahan $Z$, kita bisa mengoreksinya sebelum re-encoding dengan kode dalam, atau kita bisa mengoreksinya setelah re-encoding, dengan menerapkan gate $Z$ ke salah satu qubit dalam blok tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a circuit diagram that includes the encoding circuit and the error "
"suggested above together with the steps just described (but not the actual "
"correction step).\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah diagram Circuit yang mencakup Circuit encoding dan kesalahan "
"yang disarankan di atas bersama dengan langkah-langkah yang baru saja "
"dijelaskan (tetapi bukan langkah koreksi yang sebenarnya).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Z error detection for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-phase-error-detect-1.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Z error detection for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-phase-error-detect-1.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this particular example, the syndrome measurement is $11,$ which locates "
"the $Z$ error as having occurred on one of the qubits in the middle block.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh khusus ini, pengukuran sindrom adalah $11,$ yang menempatkan "
"kesalahan $Z$ sebagai telah terjadi pada salah satu qubit di blok tengah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One advantage of correcting $Z$ errors after the re-encoding step rather than before is that we can simplify the circuit above.\n"
"The following circuit is equivalent, but requires four fewer CNOT gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Salah satu keuntungan mengoreksi kesalahan $Z$ setelah langkah re-encoding daripada sebelumnya adalah bahwa kita bisa menyederhanakan Circuit di atas.\n"
"Circuit berikut setara, tetapi membutuhkan empat gate CNOT lebih sedikit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Simplified Z error detection for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-phase-error-detect-2.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Simplified Z error detection for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-phase-error-detect-2.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once again, the syndrome doesn't indicate which qubit has been affected by a $Z$ error, but rather which block has experienced a $Z$ error, with the effect being the same regardless of which qubit within the block was affected.\n"
"We can then correct the error by applying a $Z$ gate to any of the three qubits of whichever block was affected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekali lagi, sindrom tidak menunjukkan qubit mana yang telah terpengaruh oleh kesalahan $Z$, melainkan blok mana yang mengalami kesalahan $Z$, dengan efek yang sama terlepas dari qubit mana dalam blok yang terpengaruh.\n"
"Kita kemudian bisa mengoreksi kesalahan dengan menerapkan gate $Z$ ke salah satu dari tiga qubit dari blok mana pun yang terpengaruh.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an aside, here we see an example of *degeneracy* in a quantum error-"
"correcting code, where we're able to correct certain errors ($Z$ errors in "
"this case) without being able to identify them uniquely.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai catatan sampingan, di sini kita melihat contoh *degenerasi* dalam "
"kode koreksi kesalahan kuantum, di mana kita bisa mengoreksi kesalahan "
"tertentu (kesalahan $Z$ dalam kasus ini) tanpa bisa mengidentifikasinya "
"secara unik.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simultaneous bit- and phase-flip errors {#simultaneous-bit-and-phase-flip-"
"errors}"
msgstr ""
"Kesalahan bit-flip dan phase-flip secara bersamaan {#simultaneous-bit-and-"
"phase-flip-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've now seen how both $X$ and $Z$ errors can be detected and corrected using the 9-qubit Shor code, and in particular how at most one $X$ error or at most one $Z$ error can be detected and corrected.\n"
"Now let's suppose that both a bit-flip and a phase-flip error occur, possibly on the same qubit.\n"
"As it turns out, nothing different needs to be done in this situation from what has already been discussed —\n"
"the code is able to detect and correct up to one $X$ error and one $Z$ error simultaneously, without further modification.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang telah melihat bagaimana kesalahan $X$ dan $Z$ bisa dideteksi dan dikoreksi menggunakan kode Shor 9-Qubit, dan khususnya bagaimana paling banyak satu kesalahan $X$ atau paling banyak satu kesalahan $Z$ bisa dideteksi dan dikoreksi.\n"
"Sekarang misalkan kesalahan bit-flip dan phase-flip terjadi, mungkin pada qubit yang sama.\n"
"Ternyata, tidak ada yang berbeda yang perlu dilakukan dalam situasi ini dari apa yang sudah dibahas —\n"
"kode ini mampu mendeteksi dan mengoreksi hingga satu kesalahan $X$ dan satu kesalahan $Z$ secara bersamaan, tanpa modifikasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be more specific, $X$ errors are detected by applying the ordinary 3-bit repetition code syndrome measurement, which is performed separately on each of the three blocks of three qubits; and $Z$ errors are detected through the procedure described just above, which is equivalent to decoding the inner code, performing the syndrome measurement for the modified 3-bit repetition code for phase-flips, and then re-encoding.\n"
"These two error detection steps — as well as the corresponding corrections — can be performed completely independently of one another, and in fact it doesn't matter in which order they're performed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lebih tepatnya, kesalahan $X$ dideteksi dengan menerapkan pengukuran sindrom kode repetisi 3-bit biasa, yang dilakukan secara terpisah pada masing-masing dari tiga blok tiga qubit; dan kesalahan $Z$ dideteksi melalui prosedur yang dijelaskan tepat di atas, yang setara dengan mendekode kode dalam, melakukan pengukuran sindrom untuk kode repetisi 3-bit yang dimodifikasi untuk phase-flip, dan kemudian meng-encode ulang.\n"
"Dua langkah deteksi kesalahan ini — serta koreksi yang bersesuaian — bisa dilakukan sepenuhnya secara independen satu sama lain, dan bahkan tidak masalah urutan mana yang dilakukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see why this is, consider the example depicted in the following circuit "
"diagram, where both an $X$ and a $Z$ error have affected the bottom qubit of"
" the middle block.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk memahami mengapa ini terjadi, perhatikan contoh yang digambarkan dalam"
" diagram Circuit berikut, di mana kesalahan $X$ dan $Z$ telah mempengaruhi "
"qubit terbawah dari blok tengah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![An XZ error for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-XZ-error.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![An XZ error for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-XZ-error.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's first observe that the ordering of the errors doesn't matter, in the sense that reversing the position of the $X$ and $Z$ errors yields an equivalent circuit.\n"
"To be clear, $X$ and $Z$ do not commute, they *anti-commute*:\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita pertama-tama amati bahwa urutan kesalahan tidak masalah, dalam arti bahwa membalik posisi kesalahan $X$ dan $Z$ menghasilkan Circuit yang setara.\n"
"Untuk lebih jelasnya, $X$ dan $Z$ tidak komut, mereka *anti-komut*:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"XZ =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= - \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= -ZX.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"XZ =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= - \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= -ZX.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that the following circuit is equivalent to the one just above "
"up to a global phase factor of $-1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini berarti bahwa Circuit berikut setara dengan yang baru saja di atas "
"hingga faktor fase global $-1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A ZX error for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-ZX-error.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A ZX error for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-ZX-error.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now move the $Z$ error just like before to obtain another equivalent "
"circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang bisa memindahkan kesalahan $Z$ seperti sebelumnya untuk "
"mendapatkan Circuit setara lainnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A ZX error for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-ZX-error-2.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A ZX error for the 9-qubit Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/Shor-ZX-error-2.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point it's evident that if the procedure to detect and correct $X$ "
"errors is performed first, the $X$ error will be corrected, after which the "
"procedure for detecting and correcting $Z$ errors can be performed to "
"eliminate the $Z$ error as before.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada titik ini jelas bahwa jika prosedur untuk mendeteksi dan mengoreksi "
"kesalahan $X$ dilakukan terlebih dahulu, kesalahan $X$ akan dikoreksi, "
"setelah itu prosedur untuk mendeteksi dan mengoreksi kesalahan $Z$ bisa "
"dilakukan untuk menghilangkan kesalahan $Z$ seperti sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, the procedure to detect and correct $Z$ errors can be performed first.\n"
"The fact that this procedure works as expected, even in the presence of one or more $X$ errors, follows from the fact that $X$ gates on any of the nine qubits used for the encoding commute with all of the gates in our simplified circuit for measuring the syndrome for $Z$ errors.\n"
"Thus, this syndrome measurement will still correctly identify which block has been affected by a $Z$ error.\n"
"The fact that a $Z$ error on any block is corrected by applying a $Z$ gate to any qubit of that block, even if an $X$ error has also occurred, follows from the same argument as above concerning the ordering of $X$ and $Z$ gates giving us equivalent circuits up to a global phase.\n"
msgstr ""
"Atau, prosedur untuk mendeteksi dan mengoreksi kesalahan $Z$ bisa dilakukan terlebih dahulu.\n"
"Fakta bahwa prosedur ini berfungsi seperti yang diharapkan, bahkan dengan adanya satu atau lebih kesalahan $X$, mengikuti dari fakta bahwa gate $X$ pada salah satu dari sembilan qubit yang digunakan untuk encoding komut dengan semua gate dalam Circuit yang disederhanakan kita untuk mengukur sindrom untuk kesalahan $Z$.\n"
"Dengan demikian, pengukuran sindrom ini akan tetap mengidentifikasi dengan benar blok mana yang telah terpengaruh oleh kesalahan $Z$.\n"
"Fakta bahwa kesalahan $Z$ pada blok mana pun dikoreksi dengan menerapkan gate $Z$ ke qubit mana pun dari blok tersebut, bahkan jika kesalahan $X$ juga terjadi, mengikuti dari argumen yang sama di atas mengenai urutan gate $X$ dan $Z$ yang memberikan Circuit setara hingga fase global.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It follows that the 9-qubit Shor code can correct an $X$ error, a $Z$ error, or both, on any one of the nine qubits used for this code.\n"
"In fact, we can correct more errors than that, including multiple $X$ errors (as long as they fall into different blocks) or multiple $Z$ errors (as long as at most one block experiences an odd number of them) — but going forward, what will be most relevant for the purposes of this lesson is that we can correct an $X$ error, a $Z$ error, or both on any one qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan demikian, kode Shor 9-Qubit bisa mengoreksi kesalahan $X$, kesalahan $Z$, atau keduanya, pada salah satu dari sembilan qubit yang digunakan untuk kode ini.\n"
"Bahkan, kita bisa mengoreksi lebih banyak kesalahan dari itu, termasuk beberapa kesalahan $X$ (selama berada di blok yang berbeda) atau beberapa kesalahan $Z$ (selama paling banyak satu blok mengalami jumlah ganjil dari mereka) — tetapi ke depannya, yang paling relevan untuk tujuan pelajaran ini adalah bahwa kita bisa mengoreksi kesalahan $X$, kesalahan $Z$, atau keduanya pada satu qubit mana pun.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Error reduction for random errors {#error-reduction-for-random-errors}"
msgstr ""
"Pengurangan kesalahan untuk kesalahan acak {#error-reduction-for-random-"
"errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we move on to the last section of the lesson, which concerns "
"arbitrary quantum errors, let's briefly consider the performance of the "
"9-qubit Shor code when errors represented by Pauli matrices occur *randomly*"
" on the qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum kita beralih ke bagian terakhir pelajaran, yang berkaitan dengan "
"kesalahan kuantum sembarangan, mari kita secara singkat mempertimbangkan "
"kinerja kode Shor 9-Qubit ketika kesalahan yang direpresentasikan oleh "
"matriks Pauli terjadi *secara acak* pada qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be more concrete, let's consider a simple noise model where errors occur *independently* on the qubits, with each qubit experiencing an error with probability $p$, and with no correlation between errors on different qubits\n"
"— along similar lines to a binary symmetric channel for classical bits.\n"
"We could assign different probabilities for $X,$ $Y,$ and $Z$ errors to occur, but to keep things as simple as possible, we'll consider the worst case scenario for the 9-qubit Shor code, which is that a $Y$ error occurs on each of the affected qubits.\n"
"A $Y$ error, by the way, is equivalent (up to an irrelevant global phase factor) to both an $X$ and a $Z$ error occurring on the same qubit, given that $Y = iXZ.$\n"
"This explains our apparent disregard of $Y$ errors up to this point.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lebih konkretnya, mari kita pertimbangkan model noise sederhana di mana kesalahan terjadi *secara independen* pada qubit, dengan setiap qubit mengalami kesalahan dengan probabilitas $p$, dan tanpa korelasi antara kesalahan pada qubit yang berbeda\n"
"— sejalan dengan channel simetris biner untuk bit klasik.\n"
"Kita bisa menetapkan probabilitas yang berbeda untuk kesalahan $X,$ $Y,$ dan $Z$ yang terjadi, tetapi untuk menjaga semuanya sesederhana mungkin, kita akan mempertimbangkan skenario terburuk untuk kode Shor 9-Qubit, yaitu bahwa kesalahan $Y$ terjadi pada setiap qubit yang terpengaruh.\n"
"Omong-omong, kesalahan $Y$ setara (hingga faktor fase global yang tidak relevan) dengan kesalahan $X$ dan $Z$ yang terjadi pada qubit yang sama, mengingat bahwa $Y = iXZ.$\n"
"Ini menjelaskan pengabaian kesalahan $Y$ yang tampak hingga titik ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, supposing that $\\mathsf{Q}$ is a qubit in some particular state that we'd like to protect against errors, we can consider the option to use the 9-qubit Shor code.\n"
"A natural question to ask is, \"Should we use it?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, misalkan $\\mathsf{Q}$ adalah qubit dalam beberapa keadaan tertentu yang ingin kita lindungi dari kesalahan, kita bisa mempertimbangkan pilihan untuk menggunakan kode Shor 9-Qubit.\n"
"Pertanyaan yang wajar untuk diajukan adalah, \"Haruskah kita menggunakannya?\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is not necessarily \"yes.\"\n"
"If there's too much noise, meaning in this context that $p$ is too large, using the Shor code could actually make things worse — just like the 3-bit repetition code is worse than no code when $p$ is larger than one-half.\n"
"But, if $p$ is small enough, then the answer is \"yes,\" we should use the code, because it will decrease the likelihood that the encoded state becomes corrupted.\n"
"Let's see why this is, and what it means for $p$ to be too large or small enough for this code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jawabannya tidak selalu \"ya.\"\n"
"Jika terlalu banyak noise, artinya dalam konteks ini bahwa $p$ terlalu besar, menggunakan kode Shor sebenarnya bisa memperburuk keadaan — sama seperti kode repetisi 3-bit lebih buruk daripada tidak ada kode ketika $p$ lebih besar dari setengah.\n"
"Tetapi, jika $p$ cukup kecil, maka jawabannya adalah \"ya,\" kita harus menggunakan kode, karena akan mengurangi kemungkinan keadaan yang di-encode menjadi rusak.\n"
"Mari kita lihat mengapa ini terjadi, dan apa artinya $p$ terlalu besar atau cukup kecil untuk kode ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Shor code corrects any Pauli error on a single qubit, including a $Y$ error of course, but it doesn't properly correct two or more $Y$ errors.\n"
"To be clear, we're assuming that we're using the $X$ and $Z$ error corrections described earlier in the section.\n"
"(Of course, if we knew in advance that we only had to worry about $Y$ errors, we would naturally choose our corrections differently — but that's cheating the noise model, and we'd always be able to change the model by selecting different Pauli errors to make this new choice of corrections fail whenever two or more qubits are affected by errors.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Kode Shor mengoreksi kesalahan Pauli mana pun pada satu qubit, termasuk kesalahan $Y$ tentu saja, tetapi tidak mengoreksi dengan benar dua atau lebih kesalahan $Y$.\n"
"Untuk lebih jelasnya, kita mengasumsikan bahwa kita menggunakan koreksi kesalahan $X$ dan $Z$ yang dijelaskan sebelumnya dalam bagian.\n"
"(Tentu saja, jika kita tahu sebelumnya bahwa kita hanya perlu khawatir tentang kesalahan $Y$, kita akan secara alami memilih koreksi yang berbeda — tetapi itu curang terhadap model noise, dan kita selalu bisa mengubah model dengan memilih kesalahan Pauli yang berbeda untuk membuat pilihan koreksi baru ini gagal setiap kali dua atau lebih qubit terpengaruh oleh kesalahan.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, the code protects $\\mathsf{Q}$ so long as at most one of the nine "
"qubits is affected by an error, which happens with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, kode melindungi $\\mathsf{Q}$ selama paling banyak satu dari sembilan "
"qubit yang terpengaruh oleh kesalahan, yang terjadi dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(1-p)^9 + 9 p (1-p)^8.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(1-p)^9 + 9 p (1-p)^8.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Otherwise, with probability\n"
msgstr "Jika tidak, dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"1 - (1-p)^9 - 9 p (1-p)^8,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"1 - (1-p)^9 - 9 p (1-p)^8,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "the code fails to protect $\\mathsf{Q}.$\n"
msgstr "kode gagal melindungi $\\mathsf{Q}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Specifically, what that means in this context is that, up to a global phase, a non-identity Pauli operation will be applied to our qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ (as a logical qubit).\n"
"That is, if $X$ and $Z$ errors are detected and corrected for the Shor code as described earlier in the lesson, we'll be left with the encoding of a state that's equivalent, up to a global phase, to the encoding of a non-identity Pauli operation applied to the original state of $\\mathsf{Q}.$\n"
"A more succinct way to say this is that a *logical* error will have occurred.\n"
"That may or may not have an effect on the original state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ — or in other words the *logical qubit* we've encoded with nine *physical qubits* — but, for the sake of this analysis, we're considering this event to mean failure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Khususnya, yang dimaksud dalam konteks ini adalah bahwa, hingga fase global, operasi Pauli non-identitas akan diterapkan ke qubit kita $\\mathsf{Q}$ (sebagai qubit logis).\n"
"Artinya, jika kesalahan $X$ dan $Z$ dideteksi dan dikoreksi untuk kode Shor seperti yang dijelaskan sebelumnya dalam pelajaran, kita akan dibiarkan dengan encoding keadaan yang setara, hingga fase global, dengan encoding operasi Pauli non-identitas yang diterapkan ke keadaan asli $\\mathsf{Q}.$\n"
"Cara yang lebih ringkas untuk mengatakan ini adalah bahwa kesalahan *logis* telah terjadi.\n"
"Itu mungkin atau tidak berpengaruh pada keadaan asli $\\mathsf{Q}$ — atau dengan kata lain *qubit logis* yang telah kita encode dengan sembilan *qubit fisik* — tetapi, demi analisis ini, kita menganggap peristiwa ini sebagai kegagalan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, if we didn't bother to use the code, our one and only qubit would suffer a similar fate (of being subject to a non-identity Pauli operation) with probability $p.$\n"
"The code helps when the first probability is smaller than the second:\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sisi lain, jika kita tidak repot menggunakan kode, satu-satunya qubit kita akan mengalami nasib serupa (berupa operasi Pauli non-identitas yang diterapkan) dengan probabilitas $p.$\n"
"Kode membantu ketika probabilitas pertama lebih kecil dari yang kedua:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"1 - (1-p)^9 - 9 p (1-p)^8 < p.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"1 - (1-p)^9 - 9 p (1-p)^8 < p.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a plot that illustrates, for very small values of $p,$ that the code "
"provides an advantage, with the break-even point occurring at about "
"$0.0323.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah plot yang mengilustrasikan, untuk nilai $p$ yang sangat "
"kecil, bahwa kode memberikan keuntungan, dengan titik impas terjadi pada "
"sekitar $0.0323.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Error probability graph for independent Y errors using the Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/breakeven-Shor.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Error probability graph for independent Y errors using the Shor "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/correcting-quantum-errors/breakeven-Shor.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $p$ is smaller than this break-even point, then the code helps;\n"
"at the break-even point the probabilities are equal, so we're just wasting our time along with 8 qubits if we use the code;\n"
"and beyond the break-even point we should absolutely not be using this code because it's *increasing* the chance of a logical error on $\\mathsf{Q}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $p$ lebih kecil dari titik impas ini, maka kode membantu;\n"
"pada titik impas probabilitasnya sama, sehingga kita hanya membuang-buang waktu beserta 8 qubit jika kita menggunakan kode;\n"
"dan melewati titik impas kita sebaiknya sama sekali tidak menggunakan kode ini karena *meningkatkan* peluang kesalahan logis pada $\\mathsf{Q}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Three and a quarter percent or so may not seem like a very good break-even point, particularly when compared to $50\\%,$ which is the analogous break-even point for the 3-bit repetition code for classical information.\n"
"This difference is, in large part, due to the fact that quantum information is more delicate and harder to protect than classical information.\n"
"But also — while recognizing that the 9-qubit Shor code represents a brilliant discovery, as the world's first quantum error correcting code — it should be acknowledged that it isn't actually a very good code in practical terms.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tiga dan seperempat persen atau lebih mungkin tidak terlihat seperti titik impas yang sangat bagus, terutama bila dibandingkan dengan $50\\%,$ yang merupakan titik impas analogi untuk kode repetisi 3-bit untuk informasi klasik.\n"
"Perbedaan ini, sebagian besar, karena informasi kuantum lebih rapuh dan lebih sulit dilindungi daripada informasi klasik.\n"
"Tetapi juga — sambil mengakui bahwa kode Shor 9-Qubit merupakan penemuan brilian, sebagai kode koreksi kesalahan kuantum pertama di dunia — harus diakui bahwa sebenarnya ini bukan kode yang sangat bagus dari segi praktis.\n"
